      "doctor_question": "During those energetic, unstoppable weeks, has it ever gotten so extreme that it caused serious problems—like nearly losing your job, major conflicts, reckless spending, or needing to be hospitalized?",
      "targeted_symptom": "functional_impairment",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, it has. It definitely causes problems. At work, I was actually put on leave recently because a huge network migration I pushed through completely failed. I just moved way too fast. \n\nAnd at home... well, my wife has had to step in a lot. She has to stop me from spending too much on new equipment, or tell me to go to bed when I'm still working at 3 AM. And like I said, those conversations usually turn into arguments. \n\nIt's also messed up other parts of my life. I used to be really involved in church music, I went rock climbing, and I mentored some junior IT guys. But I've pulled away from all of that because I just can't reliably show up or follow through on anything when I'm bouncing between these extremes.",
